  "next_id": 39,
  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        0,
        -16
      ],
      "id": 38,
      "text": "Optocouplers: an infrared LED lights a phototransistor; input and output share no wire (here they share\nthe simulator's ground only). Run (F5) and click IN1 or press A: 10 mA in the LED of U1 (PC817) saturates\nits transistor, so OUT, pulled up to 3.3 V by R2, reads 0: the output is inverted. Below, a 200 Hz pulse\nthrough U2 (4N25, CTR 50 %, base pin 6 open): on the scope OUT2 is the pulse inverted, with edges of a few\nmicroseconds (10 us steps, Simulate > Settings). Lower R4 or the LED current until U2 no longer saturates."
    }
  ],
